      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐνίοτε γὰρ ἄλλαις φωναῖς τῶν ἀπὸ τῶν γραφῶν φοβερὸν καὶ δίκαιον συνίστησι θεὸν",
          "english_quote": "For sometimes, in other statements drawn from the scriptures, he establishes a fearsome and just God",
          "issue": "The draft treats τῶν ἀπὸ τῶν γραφῶν as partitive: other statements among those derived from the scriptures. That is a defensible construction, but the genitive can also mark comparison after ἄλλαις: statements different from those derived from the scriptures. This materially changes the attribution of the statements. No note identifies the construction, preserves the comparative alternative, or explains the selected reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explicitly identifying the main text’s partitive interpretation, preserving the alternative “For sometimes, with statements different from those from the scriptures, he presents a fearsome and just God,” and supplying a contextual reason for the choice. Alternatively, propose the comparative rendering as a revision and preserve the partitive reading in its note. Either revised presentation requires fresh review; the supplied print does not need correction merely because these interpretations compete.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
